        "severity": "minor",
        "evidence": "The block ends on a two-clause parallel couplet of four words each: 'Rigidity ensures convergence. Faithfulness ensures non-degeneracy at each grade.' Both restate roles already assigned in the two preceding sentences (Mostow rigidity -> total volume is a topological invariant; the proposition -> non-vanishing at each grade); the parallel-short-sentence shape is placed for quotability rather than to add content.",
        "notes": "Not fixed inline: the couplet is the paragraph's only statement of the division of labour, so deleting it loses the point and rewriting it touches the whole paragraph. Proposed: fold into the preceding sentence - 'This proposition refines that invariant into a graded series $\\{\\Phi_n(K)\\}_{n \\ge 0}$ controlled by cohomological obstructions, with rigidity supplying convergence of the series and faithfulness supplying non-degeneracy at each grade.' Separately (outside the trap axis): corollary 3's justification 'A finite polynomial cannot absorb infinitely many independent contributions.' is an assertion, not an argument, and the conclusion it supports - no polynomial relation among Vol(4_1), Vol(5_2), Vol(B_3) - is an open transcendence problem."
      }
